  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted (multiprofile) is the clear best at 0.725, and weighted fusion consistently outperforms concat across all tested pairings. However, all 8 completed experiments are multiprofile; the singleprofile dimension remains entirely untested with the top encoders. Question: config_002 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, weighted, singleprofile) tests whether removing the aggregation step (singleprofile) with the best RNA and image encoders could match or exceed the current best. Rationale: With only 1 experiment remaining after this one, this is the highest-value uncertainty to resolve—it keeps every other parameter at its empirically best setting while probing the only major unexplored axis. If it underperforms, it confirms multiprofile+transformer is essential and the last experiment can target a fine-tuning variant; if it performs competitively, it opens a new direction for the final slot."
}

